import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// PROVENANCE OF THIS ROW (a new row is a NEW node; it enters by this planning PR and is staffed
// only after the stagger check below). owner: compiler-guarantee (the lane that found and repaired
// the class, work item node://list-append-refuses-an-element-argument on the compiler-guarantee
// lane). carriers: the wall's three positional shapes are carried IN THE COMMITTED TREE as
// data strings by dag/test/claim/text_at_free_monoid_run_carrier_witness.dag via
// `wall_rows_at_parameter` over `blocking_class_census`; that witness module's claims are green by
// execution (17/17 PASS at implementation head 892a8ff9179b6f0a3afeecc654c4423365477a16, run link
// https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/16894#issuecomment-7201169375).
// THE POSITIONAL FIXTURES NAMED HERE IN AN EARLIER DRAFT DO NOT EXIST, AND NEVER DID AT THE PATH
// CLAIMED. There is no `eh_f2_pair_same_container` and no `eh_f2_repro_ticket` anywhere in the
// repository: `git ls-tree -r --name-only <ref> | grep -c eh_f2` is 0 at origin/main, 0 at this
// row's head and 0 at 892a8ff9179; `git grep -l eh_f2_pair_same_container` is 0 at origin/main, 0
// at 892a8ff9179, and 1 at this row's head -- the single hit being this file naming them. And
// `src/v1/test/claim/infer/`, where the earlier draft placed them, is not a path in the repository
// at all: `git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main -- src/v1/test/claim` prints 0 lines (rc 0), and
// `-- src/v1/test` likewise 0. What they actually were: scratch modules written at run time into
// `dag/test/claim/` by the stage-46 runner and deleted by that runner's own `trap cleanup EXIT`.
// They first ran on branch `session/eager-heron-455` at head
// 892a8ff9179b6f0a3afeecc654c4423365477a16 on srv1 (BOOT c095c0cd), in
// ~/scratch/eager-heron-455/stages3/logs46b_runner.out, which does print each leg's own exit
// status beside its census line -- the two refusals and the two accepted controls are quoted
// verbatim in the receipts below. A committed fixture per positional subject is therefore A
// CARRIER TO BE AUTHORED: one module per subject under dag/test/claim/, the refused one enrolled
// so the whole-tree fold is not broken by a subject the compiler now refuses, and its own compile
// exit status printed beside the census line it carries. Until that lands, the data-string witness
// above is the only committed carrier, and this sentence is the record that the fixtures are
// absent. updated: filed 2026-11-26 by session eager-heron-455, from the
// executed runs recorded in the receipts below (srv1, BOOT=c095c0cd, aarch64; logs41b/43/45b/46b/
// 47_runner.out under ~/scratch/eager-heron-455/stages3), and the implementation PR
// https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/16894 whose head 892a8ff9179b6f0a3afeecc654c4423365477a16
// carries the rule and whose execution receipt is
// https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/16894#issuecomment-7201169375.

// NODE PROVENANCE DEFERRED, DELIBERATELY. This row states no roadmap_node identity and mints no
// `rn_`-prefixed value: the `rn_` provenance rule is an OPEN operator question (measured at
// 8dcb8b00378: of the 1046 rows under dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode, 1045 of 1045 parseable
// `identity` values are exactly the file's own stem cast `as NonEmptyStr`, and 0 carry `rn_` — so
// identity here is the stem, as the population does, and the node-identity question is left
// unanswered rather than answered in row text). A withdrawn node identity is not carried in this
// row either; the two measured negatives below are its only record.

// STAGGER CHECK at filing (printed, not asserted): `git grep -l` for this row's stem and for its
// carrier module over origin/main and every open pull-request head; the hit counts are recorded in
// this PR's description. The swept paths and their ground file counts at origin/main, each from
// `git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main -- <path> | grep -c ""` with rc 0:
// dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode 1048, dag/test/claim 2910 (2904 of them `.dag`),
// src/v2/test/claim 1118. An earlier draft of this row also swept `src/v1/test/claim`, which has
// ZERO entries at origin/main and at this head: a sweep over a path with no files returns nothing
// whatever a sibling did there, so it is an empty grep wearing an absence's clothes and it is
// dropped from the list. If a sibling branch adds a row or a carrier naming the same class, the
// two must be joined before either is staffed.

// THE CLASS IS A READER THAT ASKS THE DECLARATION A QUESTION ABOUT THE CALL. `is this formal's type
// still an unbound variable?` has two different answers, and only one of them is about the call site:
// the container declaration's OWN parameter (`FreeMonoid`'s `T`) is unbound, always, and it is reached
// by DESCENDING a node's resolution into the type-alias expansion it resolves to. A call that passed
// `String` and settled the slot to `FreeMonoid<Primitive(String)>` therefore reads as unbound, and the
// consumer that reads it treats "unbound" as "no basis to judge", so the wrongness is SILENT: the
// argument is never compared with the declared formal at all.
data an_applied_generic_formal_is_called_unbound_through_the_declarations_own_parameter: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_applied_generic_formal_is_called_unbound_through_the_declarations_own_parameter" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder,
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundBelowTheLadder,
      ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "every direct-call argument position whose declared formal is an APPLIED generic is judged against what the argument actually produced, and the walk that descends a resolved node into the type alias' own parameters is not consulted for that position; the refusal is located at the argument and names the parameter; and each shape (refusal, same-container control, element control) is carried by a data-string subject that is ALSO compiled standalone with its own exit status printed, so a wall that stops firing shows up as red at the census rather than as a passing row"
    }
  },

  receipts: [
    "**INVALID STATE: `list_append([\"a\"], \"bc\")` at `std.algebra`'s `list_append(left: FreeMonoid<T>, right: FreeMonoid<T>)` is ACCEPTED and evaluates to `[\"a\", \"bc\"]` — a `String` reaches a `FreeMonoid<T>` parameter unchecked, at a position whose declared type the compiler has already substituted to `FreeMonoid<Primitive(String)>` (measured 2026-11-23 at main 97d114837edf, and again at origin/main 4cb919e4a109: the repro compiles and runs; the same acceptance re-measured under main's RELEASED parser at the s46 control legs). This is below the ordinary floor (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder: values inhabit declared types), and it hides the `list_push`/`list_append` mix-up authors make.**",

    "THE PREDICATE IS NOT WRONG, ITS POSITION IS. `direct_call_formal_has_unbound_type_variable` (src/v1/04_infer.dag:7910 with its recursion `_at` at :7914 on origin/main d20fa377f6c) answers whether a type tree contains an unsolved variable, and it ORs three reads at every node: the node's own inferred (via `child_type_node`), its children, and its params (via `param_node_type_expr`). Its `Resolved` arm descends into the resolution. For a nominal application that is the wrong bookkeeping: the resolution of `FreeMonoid<T>` under a `String` argument expands the alias `FreeMonoid → Empty | Cons`, and `Cons`'s cell is `Product`'s own parameter, spelled `T`. The terminal node the walk lands on has `name=\"T\"`, `kind=type_variable`, and an EMPTY inferred — it is the declaration's parameter, not the call's element. The fact the call needs lives one level ABOVE that descent, in the settled resolution the same walk had already visited and left.",

    "MEASURED, one repro, level by level, AND THE CITATION IN THE FIRST FILING WAS WRONG AND IS CORRECTED HERE: it attributed this to `S38E_*` lines in `logs41b_runner.out`, and that file does not exist (S69_LOGS41B_EXISTS=NO, log stages3/logs69_counts.out; `logs41_runner.out` does exist, 52 lines). The probe output is real and lives in `stages3/s38e_term.log` and `stages3/s38e_slot.log` on srv1 (BOOT c095c0cd, aarch64, tree 682a78edcfcde521a14681dba4d5d56e8d82b8f0, `S38E_TREE_SHA=` in s38e_slot.log). The census, one command per count with its own exit status, in stages3/logs69_counts.out: S69_TERM_LINES=28076 RC=0 terminal witness lines, S69_TERM_KIND_TYPEVAR=28076 RC=0 of them `term_kind=type_variable` -- every single one -- S69_LV4_LINES=382 RC=0 traces reaching depth LV4, S69_HERE_TV_TRUE_LINES=544 RC=0 lines carrying `here_tv=true`. One whole witness line, verbatim, is the descent this class is about: EHPROBEE|term|file=dag/std/algebra.dag|pos=5817|param=xs|declared=Node(FreeMonoid<Primitive()>)|actual=Primitive(xs)|term_depth=4|term_kind=type_variable|term_name=\"T\"|trace=LV0|kind=resolved|shape=Node(FreeMonoid<Primitive()>)|here_tv=false|n_children=1|children=[Primitive():other#false]|n_params=0|params=[] >> LV1|kind=resolved|shape=Node(FreeMonoid<Primitive()>)|here_tv=false|n_children=1|children=[Primitive():other#false]|n_params=0|params=[] >> LV2|kind=absent|shape=Coproduct(FreeMonoid)|here_tv=false|n_children=2|children=[Primitive(Empty):absent#false ; Product(Cons):absent#true]|n_params=0|params=[] >> LV3|kind=absent|shape=Product(Cons)|here_tv=false|n_children=2|children=[Primitive(T):type_variable#true ; Node(FreeMonoid<Primitive()>):absent#false]|n_params=0|params=[] >> LV4|kind=type_variable|shape=Primitive(T)|here_tv=true|n_children=0|children=[]|n_params=0|params=[] -- the terminal is the declaration's OWN `T`, reached by descending a resolved node into the container it resolves to, which is why the call site cannot see it. WITHDRAWN: the first filing said \"418 of 544 sampled terminals were reached THROUGH_ALIAS_EXPANSION\"; that token appears S69_THROUGH_ALIAS_EXPANSION=0 RC=1  <-- the row claimed 418 of 544 sampled; rc=1 means the token is absent in the log (rc 1 -- absent), and 544 is the `here_tv=true` count, not a sample, so the alias-expansion share is UNMEASURED and the mechanism claim in the header rests on the code at src/v1/04_infer.dag:7910/:7914, not on that number. THE TWO-LISTS CONTROL TRACES THE SAME PATH: `list_append([\"a\"], [\"b\"])` and `list_push([\"a\"], \"b\")` walk an identical chain, which is why no element-side rule can tell the repro from its own controls and why the repair had to be a claim about the position, not about the argument.\",",

    "FIRST MEASURED NEGATIVE, so nobody re-spends a stage on it: THE PARAM-SPELLING REPAIR IS MEASURED FALSE. The hypothesis was that the params arm reads the declaration's SPELLING (`param_node_type_expr`) where it should read the param's own inferred at leaf positions — the discipline `generic_actual_position_type` already records for the mirror-image read (its comment block is src/v1/04_env.dag:2282-2291, its declaration :2315, on origin/main d20fa377f6c). Instrument: every direct-call argument position in a named 10-module population, printing each param's spelling shape and its own inferred shape side by side. Result `S38D_PARAM_SPELLING_FLIPPED=0` over 27 403 sites with `S38D_PARAM_LEAF_SITES=27403`: ZERO params had a spelling that renders `T` while its own inferred renders the settled element. The repair was withdrawn by the lane manager on that measurement, not on argument.",

    "SECOND MEASURED NEGATIVE, same discipline: THE GLOBAL PREDICATE CHANGE. Removing the `Resolved` descent for application nodes inside the SHARED `_at` (the s39 mode3 candidate) is not a repair, it is a compiler-wide opinion. THE CITATION HERE IN THE FIRST FILING WAS WRONG AND IS CORRECTED: it attributed the figures to `S43_MEASURED_SEAM` / `S43_MEASURED_RED`, but those two lines in stages3/logs43_runner.out read S43_MEASURED_SEAM|sites_printed=0|REAL_TRUE_TOTAL=0|SCOPED_TRUE_TOTAL=0|KEPT=0|FLIPPED=0|FALSE_TO_TRUE=0|method=printed_from_S41SITE_lines and S43_MEASURED_RED|visits_printed=0|shared_true=0|scoped_true=0|flipped=0|method=printed_from_S41RED_lines -- the in-run extractor globbed `$D/census/C-*.err.keep`, which matched nothing (S63_INRUN_GLOB_MATCHES_NOTHING_RC=2), so it printed zeros; the census itself built clean (S43_BUILD_CENSUS_RC=0) and wrote 535 800 `S41SITE|` records into s43/census/C1.err..C10.err, which is what the LATER OFFLINE RECOMPUTES read. Measured now, each command's own exit status printed beside it: S66_LINES|err=535800 candidate records grepped (S66_RC_GREP|err=0), S66_UNIQUE|err=41463 distinct (file, position, parameter) sites (S66_RC_SORT|err=0), and S66_MEASURED|err|sites_unique=41463|shared_true=3490|scoped_true=160|kept=160|flipped=3330|false_to_true=0|basis=first_line_per_file_pos_param on the shard copies, with the two bases identical (S66_DIFF_BETWEEN_BASES=0 distinct-basename-lines-not-shared). Tie-break sensitivity measured, not assumed: S68_CONFLICT_TEST|unique=41463|keys_with_conflicting_records=10|of_those_shared_true_first=2|shared_true_first=3490|kept_first=160|flipped_first=3330, and with the opposite tie-break S68_TIEBREAK_LAST|unique=41463|shared_true=3492|kept=160|flipped=3332 (logs stages3/logs66_runner.out, stages3/logs68_runner.out). So the global change moves about 3 330 of 41 463 direct-call argument positions from true to FALSE and creates no refusal that was not already there (false_to_true=0). WITHDRAWN: the first filing said shared-true 3 498 and FLIPPED 3 338. Neither number appears in any log under stages3/ -- the same grep that located the zero lines above returns nothing for `FLIPPED=3338` and for `3498` -- and neither tie-break reaches them, so I cannot name their source and do not restate them. What IS reproduced exactly, on the dedup basis (recomputed from the committed census, S67_RC_AWK_DEDUP=0, over the tree at f5fb5230631d040c8d39c075ebb35676ca609e26 with S67_GUNBC_SHA256=f2f660c147cb42f610da3911cdfefb7ce7b9c3d8460ef3b6ab2c06c651c59ea0): S67_FLIPFILE_TOP_DEDUP=F|847|file=src/v2/std/compilers/target_model.dag F|393|file=src/v2/compiler/body_lowering_fold.dag F|231|file=src/v2/compiler/infer.dag F|218|file=src/v2/compiler/parse.dag F|115|file=src/v2/compiler/target_serialize.dag F|110|file=src/v2/std/grammar.dag , and per parameter S67_FLIPPARAM_TOP_DEDUP=P|1500|param=xs P|685|param=o P|261|param=left P|261|param=right P|229|param=value P|112|param=m . and that shared recursion has NINE consumers, each a named declaration in src/v1/04_infer.dag on origin/main d20fa377f6c: `optional_produced_at_required_declared` :5737, `direct_call_structured_application_mismatch_diags` :7643, `direct_call_argument_inhabitance_diags` :7801, `one_sided_non_arrow_side_is_open` :8183 and :8184, `direct_call_arg_type_mismatch` :8266, `infer_record_lit_structural` :14430 and :14443, `parameter_default_emissions` :17282 gating record-literal mismatch, structured-application mismatch, field-cardinality diagnostics and a generic-parameter branch. Turning those sites false can SILENCE refusals in eight consumers that have nothing to do with list element demands. Refused.\",",

    "THE REPAIR, AND WHY THIS SHAPE: a predicate OWNED BY THE SEAM — `element_demand_direct_call_argument_formal_is_unbound` (src/v1/04_infer.dag:8138 with its recursion `_at` at :8142 on my head 892a8ff9179, inserted after the shared `_at`, and substituted at the single consumer :7991 inside `direct_call_argument_inhabitance_diags`; mirror src/v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_infer.rs) — is substituted at ONE consumer, the direct-call argument inhabitation seam's declared-side selector. It is the shared recursion with exactly one rule changed: a node that IS an application (children non-empty) does not descend its own `Resolved` arm, because its own node is its type; a bare leaf still follows its resolution. `here`, `children` and `params` keep walking, which is why genuinely-unbound carriers survive it. The shared predicate stays byte-identical, so the other eight consumers keep today's semantics BY CONSTRUCTION.",

    "PROOF THAT THE SEAM-LOCAL RULE IS A STRICT SUBSET, not a widening. Same census, same discipline about which log says what: the in-run `S43_MEASURED_RED` line is all zeros (quoted in the previous receipt), so the red-side numbers come from the offline recompute stages3/logs63_runner.out, each count with its own exit status: S63_RED_LINES=214 `S41RED|` records, and S63_MEASURED_RED|visits_printed=214|shared_true=77|scoped_true=77|flipped=0|basis=every_printed_S41RED_line -- on every printed red line the shared read and my scoped read agree, and my read refuses none of them that the shared read does not. On the unique-site basis the same log gives S63_MEASURED_SEAM_UNIQUE|sites_unique=41463|shared_true=3490|scoped_true=160|kept=160|flipped=3330|false_to_true=0|basis=first_line_per_file_pos_param: kept 160, flipped 3 330, false_to_true=0 -- the scoped read never claims a formal is unbound where the shared read does not, so it cannot hand the declared side anywhere the basis used to win. The 160 kept shapes, grouped (stages3/logs68_runner.out, S68_RC_AWK_KEPT=0): S68_KEPT_DECLARED_TOP=D|50|declared=Primitive(T) D|40|declared=Map(...) D|15|declared=Container(List,Primitive()) D|13|declared=Primitive(K) D|9|declared=Container(List,Primitive(T)) D|5|declared=Primitive(A) D|5|declared=Primitive(V) D|4|declared=Node(Outcome<Coproduct(FreeMonoid)>) , spanning S68_KEPT_DISTINCT_DECLARED=19 distinct declared shapes and summing to the 160 kept sites exactly (S68_KEPT_TOTAL_CHECK=160); the rest is a tail of 15 shapes, the largest 9. WITHDRAWN: the first filing's \"of 5 visits to the repro's argument position, 1 shared-true stayed scoped-true and 0 flipped\" is not in any log and is replaced by the measured red census above.",

    "THE WALL, AS EXECUTED: `value does not inhabit its declared type at the direct call argument for parameter 'right' [RefusedTextAtRunOfNonCharElement: a Text value is passed at a Run-of-non-Char element demand: the element is not Char and Text is not a Run carrier]: declared 'Node(FreeMonoid<Primitive(String)>)', produced 'Primitive(String)'` at a located `file:line:col` (dag/test/claim/eh_f2_pair_same_container.dag:14:69, a position with no symbol beside it by necessity: the subject is a data string compiled at run time, not a declaration). It took TWO arms to fire, and that is the class's second lesson: the element demand must be armed by a `Run`-shaped declared element (`run_element_demand`) as well as by the carrier, because `FreeMonoid<T>`'s element is `T` — neither the carrier nor the element alone distinguishes the repro from `list_append([\"a\"], [\"b\"])`.",

    "OBSERVATION THAT MADE IT MEASURABLE: a subject whose call the compiler now REFUSES cannot be carried by a `test fn` claim module, because the module fails to fold before any claim runs -- the fold, not the claim, is where the refusal lands. The three positional subjects (`list_append([\"a\"], \"bc\")` refused; `list_append([\"a\"], [\"b\"])` and `list_push([\"a\"], \"b\")` accepted) are carried instead as DATA STRINGS inside a census-probe witness (dag/test/claim/text_at_free_monoid_run_carrier_witness.dag, `wall_rows_at_parameter` over `blocking_class_census`), carried as DATA STRINGS. THE FIXTURES THIS SENTENCE NAMED IN THE FIRST FILING ARE ABSENT AND ARE A CARRIER TO BE AUTHORED: `eh_f2_pair_same_container` and `eh_f2_repro_ticket` exist in no revision of this repository and never lived under `src/v1/test/claim/infer/`, which is not a path at all (counts in the header above); they were written into `dag/test/claim/` at run time and deleted by the runner's own cleanup trap. They first ran on branch `session/eager-heron-455` at head 892a8ff9179b6f0a3afeecc654c4423365477a16, srv1 BOOT c095c0cd, in stages3/logs46b_runner.out, and that log does keep the obligation this row demands -- the subject's own compile exit status printed beside its census line: S46_LEGS|PAIR_SAME_CONTAINER|module=dag/test/claim/eh_f2_pair_same_container.dag|want=hard|REAL_EXIT=1|hard=2|arm=2|names_param_right=11, S46_LEGS|TICKET_REPRO|module=dag/test/claim/eh_f2_repro_ticket.dag|want=hard|REAL_EXIT=1|hard=2|arm=2|names_param_right=10, and the two accepted controls S46_LEGS|TWO_LISTS|module=dag/test/claim/eh_f2_control_two_lists.dag|want=accept|REAL_EXIT=0|hard=0|arm=0|names_param_none=0, S46_LEGS|LIST_PUSH|module=dag/test/claim/eh_f2_control_list_push.dag|want=accept|REAL_EXIT=0|hard=0|arm=0|names_param_none=0. The same five subjects against main's RELEASED parser are accepted, as they must be before the wall is credited: S46_LEGS|MAIN_RELEASED_PAIR_SAME_CONTAINER|module=dag/test/claim/eh_f2_pair_same_container.dag|want=accept|REAL_EXIT=0|hard=0|arm=0|names_param_none=0. So the positional carriers in the COMMITTED TREE today are the data strings in dag/test/claim/text_at_free_monoid_run_carrier_witness.dag, whose weakness is stated plainly: a data-string subject can silently stop compiling and still print a row, which is why the committed fixture above is the thing to author nex",

    "ATTRIBUTION, measured rather than assumed: of three candidate variants, only the seam-local selector refuses the repro; swapping the element read inside `run_element_demand` alone (V2) is measured irrelevant measured in stages3/logs42_runner.out, where the V2 patch is applied, built and reverted with its own exit statuses (S41_V2_APPLIED=1, S42_BUILD_V2_RC=0, binary S42_BIN_V2_SHA=1fded00a93ef8daa18ad666dbe7e6c70e7f9a8174b8428ac469fa38dc8b7636c, S42_LEGS_V2_RC=0, S42_REVERT_V2_RC=0), and under V2 the repro's own leg ACCEPTS it: S42_v2S37_LEG_PAIR_SAME_CONTAINER_REAL_EXIT=0, S42_v2S37_LEG_PAIR_SAME_CONTAINER_hard_lines=0, the runner's own label S42_v2S37_LEG_PAIR_SAME_CONTAINER_VERDICT=AS-EXPECTED, and the global predicate (V3) is the refused one. The layer rule matters for any reader who re-runs this: the binary compiles the COMMITTED generated Rust, so a `.dag`-only edit is inert — the `.dag` half and the regenerated mirror half must BOTH land, and the mirror is emitter output (one heal round, `--required-regen --regen-emission-scope-carried --base-mirror --regen-affected-scope`, run twice with equal mirror sha e0e93afe46de7fd50b7cb2c97a491aca029b999be1eabbca83ddd532d4545438 on 2026-11-26, srv1 BOOT=c095c0cd, log stages3/logs45b_runner.out).",
    "WHICH ROUTE PRODUCED WHICH VERDICT FOR THIS ROW ITSELF, so a green never means more than it does: the derived-roster join claim `the_native_recurring_failure_mode_roster_agrees_with_the_seeds` (src/v2/test/claim/derived_roster_seed_agreement.dag) EVALUATED `true` with this row present, and it did so by the RUN ROUTE (`gunbc run --entry <module> --function <name>`, head-built binary f2f660c147cb) -- so it is a run-route EVALUATION, not a PASS line; its rc 2 and its host complaint (`returned `true`, not `ProcessExit``) are the host mapping a verdict to an exit code, not a refusal by gunbc. The `gunbc test` route REFUSED both arms, with and without the row, at rc 2 (S52_REAL_EXIT|A_no_row=2, S52_REAL_EXIT|B_with_row=2), and the refusal text -- quoted verbatim from the per-leg logs, which is where it lives, not in the runner log -- is gunbc test: REFUSED cause=BinaryFreshnessUndecided — /home/briansrls/scratch/eager-heron-455/gunbc/target/release/gunbc: its dep-info names an input outside this worktree (/home/briansrls/scratch/eager-heron-455/gunbc); it was built from another checkout, so nothing here says whether it answers for this one Nothing on this row is claimed as a CI PASS line; the claim route over this row belongs to the staffing round, and the witness tier for this filing is parses + typechecks. Measured 2026-11-26 on srv1 (BOOT c095c0cd, aarch64). THE FILES ARE NAMED AS THEY ARE, because the first filing named a set that did not contain two of these claims: the run-route evaluation line is S60C| error: function `the_native_recurring_failure_mode_roster_agrees_with_the_seeds` returned `true`, not `ProcessExit`. in stages3/logs60_runner.out (and S59C| error: function `the_native_recurring_failure_mode_roster_agrees_with_the_seeds` returned `true`, not `ProcessExit`. in stages3/logs59_runner.out, the round that verified the committed bytes were the edited ones, S59_BLOB_IS_THE_EDITED_BYTES=yes); the test-route refusals are s52/A_no_row.log and s52/B_with_row.log with their exit statuses in stages3/logs52_runner.out (S52_REAL_EXIT|A_no_row=2, binary S52_BIN_SHA=f2f660c147cb42f610da3911cdfefb7ce7b9c3d8460ef3b6ab2c06c651c59ea0, tree S52_TREE_SHA=bc9f1a1b3e4730caf5e38da4c66eafa305b6780f).",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
